---
import:
  - typescript-react-app-template # spec source available at https://github.com/Codeplain-ai/codeplain/blob/main/standard_template_library/
requires:
  - typescript-react-app-boilerplate # spec source available at https://github.com/Codeplain-ai/codeplain/blob/main/standard_template_library/
---

***definitions***

- :User: is the user of :App:

- :Task: describes an activity that needs to be done by :User:. :Task: has the following attributes
  - Name - a short description of :Task:. This is a required attribute. The name must be at least 3 characters long.
  - Notes - additional details about :Task:
  - Due Date - optional date by which :User: is supposed to complete :Task:.

- :TaskList: is a list of :Task: items.
  - Initially :TaskList: should be empty.

***implementation reqs***
> Implementation requirements are defined in 'typescript-react-app-template'.

***test reqs***
> Test requirements are defined in 'typescript-react-app-template'.

***functional specs***

> Every functionality starts with a '# <func-id>' heading. The test scenarios of a
> functionality live in the test plain file tests/task-manager/<func-id>.plain.
> The required module 'typescript-react-app-boilerplate' brings its own functionality,
> so it has a test plain file too: tests/typescript-react-app-boilerplate/entry-point.plain.

# app-header
:App: shows its header. The details of the user interface are provided in the file [task_list_ui_specification.yaml](task_list_ui_specification.yaml).

# show-task-list
:App: shows :TaskList:. The details of the user interface are provided in the file [task_list_ui_specification.yaml](task_list_ui_specification.yaml).

# add-task
A :User: can add a :Task:. Only valid :Task: items are added. The details of the user interface are provided in the file [add_new_task_modal_specification.yaml](add_new_task_modal_specification.yaml).

# delete-task
A :User: can delete a :Task:.

# edit-task
A :User: can edit a :Task:.

# complete-task
A :User: can mark a :Task: as completed.



> see https://www.plainlang.org/ for more information on ***plain
